.TH PDFBOOKMARKS 1 "October 2026" "pdfbookmarks" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pdfbookmarks \- add a hierarchical bookmark outline to a PDF
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pdfbookmarks
.I file.pdf
.RB [ \-m | \-\-markdown
.IR file.md ]
.RB [ \-o | \-\-output
.IR out.pdf ]
.RB [ \-n | \-\-dry\-run ]
.RB [ \-v | \-\-verbose ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pdfbookmarks
adds a PDF outline (the bookmarks shown in the side panel of Preview or
Acrobat) to a PDF that has none.
PDFs exported from iA Writer through the macOS Quartz PDF engine contain no
bookmarks, even though the document has a clear heading structure.
The visible content of the PDF is not changed.
.PP
The headings come from one of two sources, chosen in this order:
.IP 1. 3
The Markdown file given with
.BR \-m ;
.IP 2. 3
A Markdown file next to the PDF with the same base name and a
.B .md
extension, if it exists.
.PP
If neither is available, the headings are detected from the font sizes in
the PDF.
.SS Markdown mode
ATX headings (\fB#\fR to \fB######\fR) are read from the Markdown source,
ignoring fenced code blocks.
Trailing \fB#\fR characters, MultiMarkdown labels (\fB[Label]\fR), emphasis
markers, inline code marks and link syntax are removed from the heading text.
Each heading is then searched in the text of the PDF, sequentially: the search
for a heading starts just after the previous match.
Comparison is made on normalized text (Unicode NFKC, so ligatures are
expanded; soft hyphens removed; typographic apostrophes unified; case
ignored).
A heading matches a line that consists of the heading alone, or up to three
consecutive lines of the same font size (a heading that wraps).
Lines larger than the body text are preferred.
Headings that are not found are skipped (a warning is printed with
.BR \-v ).
The outline level is the number of \fB#\fR characters, adjusted so that the
first entry is level 1 and a level never increases by more than one.
.SS Font-size mode
The body size is the most frequent font size.
Lines larger than the body size by more than 4% are headings; each distinct
size, from the largest, gives levels 1, 2, 3 (up to 6).
The largest size is the document title only if its first group of lines is at
the top of the first page; later lines of that size (authors, affiliations)
are not headings.
A standalone line reading
.IR Abstract ,
.I Riassunto
or
.I Sommario
is added one level below the title.
Consecutive heading lines of the same size are merged (wrapped titles).
Text smaller than 8 pt, digits-only lines and the top and bottom 70 pt of
each page are ignored.
.PP
Every bookmark points to the page and to the position of the heading.
An existing outline is replaced.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I file.pdf
The PDF to process.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-markdown " " \fIfile.md\fR
Take the headings from this Markdown file.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIout.pdf\fR
Write the result to
.I out.pdf
and leave the input file untouched.
By default the PDF is modified in place: the new file is written to a
temporary file in the same directory and then atomically moved over the
original, so a half-written file is never left behind.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Print the outline that would be created (level, page, title) and write
nothing.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Print details, including the outline and warnings about headings not found.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the help text (in Italian) and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
Add bookmarks in place after exporting from iA Writer, using the Markdown
file with the same name:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ pdfbookmarks ~/Documents/article.pdf
.fi
.RE
.PP
Preview the outline using an explicit Markdown file:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ pdfbookmarks -n -m ~/Documents/article.md ~/Desktop/export.pdf
.fi
.RE
.PP
Keep the original and write a bookmarked copy, detecting headings from font
sizes:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ pdfbookmarks -o article-indexed.pdf article.pdf
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success (also for \fB\-n\fR).
.TP
.B 1
Error: file missing, not a PDF, encrypted PDF, Markdown file missing, or no
headings found.
.SH NOTES
Matching is sequential: headings must appear in the PDF in the same order as
in the Markdown source.
Duplicate titles are therefore handled in order of appearance, but a heading
out of order may be skipped.
.PP
The tool needs PyMuPDF, which is installed system-wide with
.BR "/Library/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/3.13/bin/pip3 install pymupdf" ;
it uses no external commands and works with
a minimal
.BR PATH .
.PP
An existing outline is always replaced.
Messages are printed in Italian.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pdfinfo (1),
.BR qpdf (1),
.BR mutool (1)
